# A CONTAINER'S COUNTERS ARE NATIVE METHODS, read through an instance. A method
# read through an instance has no reference form, so it is called, and a marker
# after it applies to the count it answers -- which is a value, not a place, so
# `.take` of it is refused. `length`, `capacity` and `size` were once typed as
# plain u64 members, and `.take` of one reached the C as `z_v3.length.take`,
# which the C compiler refused. (A native's own refusal: native_take_ref.)
main: function is {
    xs: ListVal i64
    m: (MapVV k: i64 v: i64)
    ids: (IdSet u32)
    arr: (array t: i64 to: 4)
    raw: (str to: 8)
    a: xs.length.take
    b: xs.capacity.take
    c: m.length.take
    d: ids.capacity.take
    e: arr.length.take
    f: raw.size.take
    print "\{xs.length}"
}
